  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1119 PM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nAfter a cold start to the morning on Sunday, temperatures will \nsteadily warm with highs forecast in the mid 60s to near 70. Another \nchilly morning is forecast on Monday (although not as cold as Sunday \nmorning) with lows in the 40s. Highs on Monday will be in the 70s. \n\nAn upper level ridge is forecast to strengthen across Texas Tuesday \nthrough Thursday. This will result in above normal temperatures and \ngenerally dry conditions. Highs on Tuesday will be in the mid 70s to \nnear 80. Highs the rest of the work week will be in the 80s. \nOvernight lows will be in the 50s to lower 60s. The next upper level \ntrough is forecast to approach the forecast area from the west \nFriday into next weekend. This may bring the next chance of showers \nand thunderstorms to the area. For now, have kept low rain chances \n(15-20%) across the area on Friday given the uncertainty this far \nout.",
